{"id":"mahabharata-6-081","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":81,"title":"एकाशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 81 · Seventh day: Arjuna and Bhishma","summary":{"en":"Arjuna cuts down the kings who attack him, and Duryodhana taunts Bhishma into fighting harder. Bhishma shatters Arjuna's bow and banner, and Pandava warriors cheer as Arjuna's club strikes down a chariot.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನ ತನ್ನ ಮೇಲೆ ಬರುವ ರಾಜರನ್ನು ಕಡಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಚುಚ್ಚಿ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಹೋರಾಡಲು ಪ್ರೇರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಬಿಲ್ಲು, ಧ್ವಜ ಮುರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಗದೆ ರಥವನ್ನು ಬಡಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन आक्रमण करने वाले राजाओं को काट देते हैं, और दुर्योधन ताना देकर भीष्म को अधिक लड़ने को उकसाता है। भीष्म अर्जुन का धनुष और ध्वज तोड़ देते हैं, और अर्जुन की गदा एक रथ को गिरा देती है।","te":"తనపైకి వచ్చే రాజులను అర్జునుడు నరుకుతాడు; దుర్యోధనుడు భీష్ముని సూటిగా అని మరింత పోరాడమని ప్రేరేపిస్తాడు. భీష్ముడు అర్జునుని విల్లు, ధ్వజాన్ని ఛేదిస్తాడు; అర్జునుని గద ఒక రథాన్ని కూల్చుతుంది.","ta":"தன்னைத் தாக்கும் மன்னர்களை அர்ஜுனன் வெட்டுகிறான்; துரியோதனன் பீஷ்மரை இகழ்ந்து மேலும் போரிடத் தூண்டுகிறான். பீஷ்மர் அர்ஜுனனின் வில்லையும் கொடியையும் முறிக்க, அர்ஜுனனின் கதை ஒரு தேரை வீழ்த்துகிறது.","ml":"തന്നെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്ന രാജാക്കന്മാരെ അർജുനൻ വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു; കൂടുതൽ കഠിനമായി പൊരുതാൻ ദുര്യോധനൻ ഭീഷ്മരെ പരിഹസിക്കുന്നു. ഭീഷ്മർ അർജുനന്റെ വില്ലും കൊടിയും തകർക്കുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെ ഗദ ഒരു രഥത്തെ തകർക്കുമ്പോൾ പാണ്ഡവ യോദ്ധാക്കൾ ആർത്തുവിളിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.81; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स तुद्यमानस्तु शरैर्धनंजयः\nपदा हतो नाग इव श्वसन्बली ।\nबाणेन बाणेन महारथानां\nचिच्छेद चापानि रणे प्रसह्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pricked by their arrows, Dhananjaya, strong, breathed hard like an elephant struck by a foot, and forcefully cut the bows of the great chariot-warriors in the battle, one arrow for each."}},{"n":2,"text":"संछिद्य चापानि च तानि राज्ञां\nतेषां रणे वीर्यवतां क्षणेन ।\nविव्याध बाणैर्युगपन्महात्मा\nनिःशेषतां तेष्वथ मन्यमानः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having cut the bows of those mighty kings in a moment, the great-souled Arjuna struck them all at once with arrows, thinking to finish them off."}},{"n":3,"text":"निपेतुराजौ रुधिरप्रदिग्धा-\nस्ते ताडिताः शक्रसुतेन राजन् ।\nविभिन्नगात्राः पतितोत्तमाङ्गा\nगतासवश्छिन्नतनुत्रकायाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by Indra's son, O king, they fell in the battle smeared with blood, their bodies torn, heads fallen, lifeless, their armor and bodies cut open."}},{"n":4,"text":"महीं गताः पार्थबलाभिभूता\nविचित्ररूपा युगपद्विनेशुः ।\nदृष्ट्वा हतांस्तान्युधि राजपुत्रां-\nस्त्रिगर्तराजः प्रययौ क्षणेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fallen to the ground, overcome by Partha's might, they perished all at once in many different shapes. Seeing those princes slain in the battle, the king of the Trigartas fled in a moment."}},{"n":5,"text":"तेषां रथानामथ पृष्ठगोपा\nद्वात्रिंशदन्येऽब्यपतन्त पार्थम् ।\nतथैव ते संपरिवार्य पार्थं\nविकृष्य चापानि महारवाणि ।\nअवीवृषन्बाणमहौघवृष्ट्या\nयथा गिरिं तोयधरा जलौघैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then thirty-two others who guarded the rear of those chariots fell upon Partha. Surrounding him and drawing their loud-twanging bows, they rained a great flood of arrows on him, as clouds pour floods of water on a mountain."}},{"n":6,"text":"संपीड्यमानस्तु शरौघवृष्ट्या\nधनंजयस्तान्युधि जातरोषः ।\nषष्ट्या शरैः संयति तैलधौतै-\nर्जघान तानप्यथ पृष्ठगोपान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hard pressed by that rain of arrows, Dhananjaya, angered in the battle, killed those rear-guards too with sixty arrows washed in oil."}},{"n":7,"text":"षष्टिं रथांस्तानवजित्य संख्ये\nधनंजयः प्रीतमना यशस्वी ।\nअथात्वरद्भीष्मवधाय जिष्णु-\nर्बलानि राज्ञां समरे निहत्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated those sixty chariot-fighters in the battle, the famous Dhananjaya was pleased. Then Jishnu, having struck down the kings' forces in the fight, hurried toward the killing of Bhishma."}},{"n":8,"text":"त्रिगर्तराजो निहतान्समीक्ष्य\nमहारथांस्तानथ बन्धुवर्गान् ।\nरणे पुरस्कृत्य नराधिपांस्ता-\nञ्जगाम पार्थं त्वरितो वधाय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his great chariot-warriors and kinsmen slain, the king of the Trigartas put the other kings in front in the battle and went quickly to kill Partha."}},{"n":9,"text":"अभिद्रुतं चास्त्रभृतां वरिष्ठं\nधनंजयं वीक्ष्य शिखण्डिमुख्याः ।\nअभ्युद्ययुस्ते शितशस्त्रहस्ता\nरिरक्षिषन्तो रथमर्जुनस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Dhananjaya, best of weapon-bearers, attacked, Shikhandi and the others with sharp weapons in their hands went out to meet them, wanting to protect Arjuna's chariot."}},{"n":10,"text":"पार्थोऽपि तानापततः समीक्ष्य\nत्रिगर्तराज्ञा सहितान्नृवीरान् ।\nविध्वंसयित्वा समरे धनुष्मा-\nन्गाण्डीवमुक्तैर्निशितैः पृषत्कैः ।\nभीष्मं यियासुर्युधि संददर्श\nदुर्योधनं सैन्धवादींश्च राज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, seeing those heroes with the king of the Trigartas coming at him, destroyed them in the battle with sharp arrows shot from the Gandiva. Wishing to go on to Bhishma, he saw Duryodhana and the other kings, Saindhava among them."}},{"n":11,"text":"आवारयिष्णूनभिसंप्रयाय\nमुहूर्तमायोध्य बलेन वीरः ।\nउत्सृज्य राजानमनन्तवीर्यो\nजयद्रथादींश्च नृपान्महौजाः ।\nययौ ततो भीमबलो मनस्वी\nगाङ्गेयमाजौ शरचापपाणिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Advancing on those who tried to hold him back and fighting them for a moment with his force, that hero of boundless strength and great vigor left the king and Jayadratha and the rest, and, terrible in might and determined, went with bow and arrows in hand to the son of Ganga in the battle."}},{"n":12,"text":"युधिष्ठिरश्चोग्रबलो महात्मा\nसमाययौ त्वरितो जातकोपः ।\nमद्राधिपं समभित्यज्य संख्ये\nस्वभागमाप्तं तमनन्तकीर्तिः ।\nसार्धं स माद्रीसुतभीमसेनै-\nर्भीष्मं ययौ शांतनवं रणाय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira too, great-souled and fierce in strength, came quickly in anger. Leaving the king of Madra, whom he had met as his share in the battle, that man of boundless fame went with the sons of Madri and Bhimasena to fight Bhishma, son of Shantanu."}},{"n":13,"text":"तैः संप्रयुक्तः स महारथाग्र्यै-\nर्गङ्गासुतः समरे चित्रयोधी ।\nन विव्यथे शांतनवो महात्मा\nसमागतैः पाण्डुसुतैः समस्तैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Set on by those foremost great chariot-warriors, Ganga's son, a varied fighter in the battle, the great-souled son of Shantanu, was not shaken by all the Pandavas who had come together."}},{"n":14,"text":"अथैत्य राजा युधि सत्यसंधो\nजयद्रथोऽत्युग्रबलो मनस्वी ।\nचिच्छेद चापानि महारथानां\nप्रसह्य तेषां धनुषा वरेण ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Jayadratha, true to his word, of terrible strength and resolve, came and forcibly cut the bows of those great chariot-warriors with his excellent bow."}},{"n":15,"text":"युधिष्ठिरं भीमसेनं यमौ च\nपार्थं तथा युधि संजातकोपः ।\nदुर्योधनः क्रोधविषो महात्मा\nजघान बाणैरनलप्रकाशैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, great-souled and with poison in his anger, enraged, struck Yudhishthira, Bhima, the twins and Partha in the battle with arrows bright as fire."}},{"n":16,"text":"कृपेण शल्येन शलेन चैव\nतथा विभो चित्रसेनेन चाजौ ।\nविद्धाः शरैस्तेऽतिविवृद्धकोपै-\nर्देवा यथा दैत्यगणैः समेतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by Kripa, Shalya, Shala and Chitrasena, O lord, in the battle, with their rage greatly swollen, they seemed like gods against assembled hosts of daityas."}},{"n":17,"text":"छिन्नायुधं शांतनवेन राजा\nशिखण्डिनं प्रेक्ष्य च जातकोपः ।\nअजातशत्रुः समरे महात्मा\nशिखण्डिनं क्रुद्ध उवाच वाक्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king left with his weapons cut by Shantanu's son, and seeing Shikhandi, the great-souled Ajatashatru was angered and in wrath spoke to him in the battle."}},{"n":18,"text":"उक्त्वा तथा त्वं पितुरग्रतो मा-\nमहं हनिष्यामि महाव्रतं तम् ।\nभीष्मं शरौघैर्विमलार्कवर्णैः\nसत्यं वदामीति कृता प्रतिज्ञा ॥","meaning":{"en":"You said before your father, \"I will kill that man of great vows, Bhishma, with floods of arrows bright as the pure sun; I tell the truth,\" and thus made your vow."}},{"n":19,"text":"त्वया न चैनां सफलां करोषि\nदेवव्रतं यन्न निहंसि युद्धे ।\nमिथ्याप्रतिज्ञो भव मा नृवीर\nरक्षस्व धर्मं च कुलं यशश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"You do not make that vow come true, since you do not kill Devavrata in battle. Do not be one whose vow was false, hero among men. Guard your duty, your family and your fame."}},{"n":20,"text":"प्रेक्षस्व भीष्मं युधि भीमवेगं\nसर्वांस्तपन्तं मम सैन्यसंघान् ।\nशरौघजालैरतितिग्मतेजैः\nकालं यथा मृत्युकृतं क्षणेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at Bhishma in the battle, of terrible speed, burning all my armies with his nets of floods of arrows of fierce brilliance, like Time, the maker of death, in a moment."}},{"n":21,"text":"निकृत्तचापः समरानपेक्षः\nपराजितः शांतनवेन राज्ञा ।\nविहाय बन्धूनथ सोदरांश्च\nक्व यास्यसे नानुरूपं तवेदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With your bow cut, indifferent to the battle, defeated by King Shantanu's son, where will you go, leaving your relatives and brothers? This does not befit you."}},{"n":22,"text":"दृष्ट्वा हि भीष्मं तमनन्तवीर्यं\nभग्नं च सैन्यं द्रवमाणमेवम् ।\nभीतोऽसि नूनं द्रुपदस्य पुत्र\nतथा हि ते मुखवर्णोऽप्रहृष्टः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bhishma of boundless strength and the army broken and fleeing, you are surely afraid, son of Drupada, for your face has lost its color and cheer."}},{"n":23,"text":"आज्ञायमानेऽपि धनंजयेन\nमहाहवे संप्रसक्ते नृवीर ।\nकथं हि भीष्मात्प्रथितः पृथिव्यां\nभयं त्वमद्य प्रकरोषि वीर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even though Dhananjaya is known to be here, hero among men, in this great fight, how is it that you, famed throughout the earth, are afraid of Bhishma today?"}},{"n":24,"text":"स धर्मराजस्य वचो निशम्य\nरूक्षाक्षरं विप्रलापानुबद्धम् ।\nप्रत्यादेशं मन्यमानो महात्मा\nप्रतत्वरे भीष्मवधाय राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the harsh words of the king of dharma, full of reproach, the great-souled Shikhandi took it as a command, and hurried to kill Bhishma, O king."}},{"n":25,"text":"तमापतन्तं महता जवेन\nशिखण्डिनं भीष्ममभिद्रवन्तम् ।\nआवारयामास हि शल्य एनं\nशस्त्रेण घोरेण सुदुर्जयेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Shikhandi came rushing at Bhishma with great speed, Shalya blocked him with a terrible, almost unconquerable weapon."}},{"n":26,"text":"स चापि दृष्ट्वा समुदीर्यमाण-\nमस्त्रं युगान्ताग्निसमप्रभावम् ।\nनासौ व्यमुह्यद्द्रुपदस्य पुत्रो\nराजन्महेन्द्रप्रतिमप्रभावः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Drupada, seeing that weapon rising with a blaze like the fire at the end of an age, was not bewildered, O king, for his power was like great Indra's."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्थौ च तत्रैव महाधनुष्मा-\nञ्शरैस्तदस्त्रं प्रतिबाधमानः ।\nअथाददे वारुणमन्यदस्त्रं\nशिखण्ड्यथोग्रं प्रतिघाताय तस्य ।\nतदस्त्रमस्त्रेण विदार्यमाणं\nखस्थाः सुरा ददृशुः पार्थिवाश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He stood there, that great bowman, warding off that weapon with arrows. Then Shikhandi took up another weapon, the fierce Varuna weapon, to counter it. The gods in the sky and the kings saw that weapon being split by weapon."}},{"n":28,"text":"भीष्मस्तु राजन्समरे महात्मा\nधनुः सुचित्रं ध्वजमेव चापि ।\nछित्त्वानदत्पाण्डुसुतस्य वीरो\nयुधिष्ठिरस्याजमीढस्य राज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Bhishma, great-souled hero, in the battle cut the bow and the banner of the Pandava, King Yudhishthira, descendant of Ajamidha, and roared."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततः समुत्सृज्य धनुः सबाणं\nयुधिष्ठिरं वीक्ष्य भयाभिभूतम् ।\nगदां प्रगृह्याभिपपात संख्ये\nजयद्रथं भीमसेनः पदातिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, throwing aside his bow and arrows, was overcome with fear, and Bhimasena, taking his mace, attacked Jayadratha on foot in the battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"तमापतन्तं महता जवेन\nजयद्रथः सगदं भीमसेनम् ।\nविव्याध घोरैर्यमदण्डकल्पैः\nशितैः शरैः पञ्चशतैः समन्तात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Bhimasena with his mace came at him with great speed, Jayadratha struck him all around with five hundred sharp, terrible arrows like Yama's staffs."}},{"n":31,"text":"अचिन्तयित्वा स शरांस्तरस्वी\nवृकोदरः क्रोधपरीतचेताः ।\nजघान वाहान्समरे समस्ता-\nनारट्टजान्सिन्धुराजस्य संख्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Paying no heed to the arrows, Vrikodara, his mind seized with rage, killed all the Aratta-bred horses of the king of the Sindhus in the battle."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततोऽभिवीक्ष्याप्रतिमप्रभाव-\nस्तवात्मजस्त्वरमाणो रथेन ।\nअभ्याययौ भीमसेनं निहन्तुं\nसमुद्यतास्त्रः सुरराजकल्पः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your son of matchless power, seeing this, hastened on his chariot to kill Bhimasena, with weapon raised like the king of the gods."}},{"n":33,"text":"भीमोऽप्यथैनं सहसा विनद्य\nप्रत्युद्ययौ गदया तर्जमानः ।\nसमुद्यतां तां यमदण्डकल्पां\nदृष्ट्वा गदां ते कुरवः समन्तात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, roaring suddenly, went to meet him, threatening him with his mace. Seeing that mace raised like Yama's staff, the Kauravas on every side"}},{"n":34,"text":"विहाय सर्वे तव पुत्रमुग्रं\nपातं गदायाः परिहर्तुकामाः ।\nअपक्रान्तास्तुमुले संविमर्दे\nसुदारुणे भारत मोहनीये ॥","meaning":{"en":"left your fierce son, wanting to escape the fall of the mace, and drew away in that tumultuous, terrible, bewildering crush, O Bharata."}},{"n":35,"text":"अमूढचेतास्त्वथ चित्रसेनो\nमहागदामापतन्तीं निरीक्ष्य ।\nरथं समुत्सृज्य पदातिराजौ\nप्रगृह्य खड्गं विमलं च चर्म ।\nअवप्लुतः सिंह इवाचलाग्रा-\nज्जगाम चान्यं भुवि भूमिदेशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Chitrasena, with clear mind, seeing the great mace coming, abandoned his chariot, took a sword and bright shield, and on foot leapt away like a lion from a mountain peak, going to another place on the ground."}},{"n":36,"text":"गदापि सा प्राप्य रथं सुचित्रं\nसाश्वं ससूतं विनिहत्य संख्ये ।\nजगाम भूमिं ज्वलिता महोल्का\nभ्रष्टाम्बराद्गामिव संपतन्ती ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mace, reaching his fine chariot, with its horses and charioteer, destroyed it in the battle and fell to the earth like a great blazing meteor falling from the sky to the ground."}},{"n":37,"text":"आश्चर्यभूतं सुमहत्त्वदीया\nदृष्ट्वैव तद्भारत संप्रहृष्टाः ।\nसर्वे विनेदुः सहिताः समन्ता-\nत्पुपूजिरे तव पुत्रं ससैन्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that great wonder, O Bharata, your men were overjoyed; all cried out together on every side and honored your son along with his army."}}]}]}